===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker- (turn)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|ryng}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hring||ring, circle}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hring}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hringaz||ring}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)krengʰ-}}, extended nasalized form of {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||to turn, bend}}. {{doublet|en|rank|rink}}.

